==Rules==
{{ColosseumRule|Mega Cat Cannon|200}}

==Battleground==
*2 [[Sir Seal]]s spawn after 3.33 seconds<sup>100f</sup>, delay 33.33~40 seconds<sup>1,000f~1,200f</sup>.
*2 [[Relic Doge]]s spawn after 10 seconds<sup>300f</sup>, delay 20~26.67 seconds<sup>600f~800f</sup>.
*2 [[Aku Doge]]s spawn after 16.67 seconds<sup>500f</sup>, delay 20~26.67 seconds<sup>600f~800f</sup>.
*1 [[Aku Gory]] spawns after 26.67 seconds<sup>800f</sup>.
*When the base reaches 99% HP:
**1 [[Berserkory]] spawns as the boss.
**2 [[Le'Behemoth]]s spawn, delay 93.33~100 seconds<sup>2,800f~3,000f</sup>.
**5 [[Loris|Lorises]] spawn after 3.33 seconds<sup>100f</sup>, delay 30~36.67 seconds<sup>900f~1,100f</sup>.
**1 [[Aku Gory]] spawns after 6.67 seconds<sup>200f</sup>.
**2 [[Othom]]s spawn after 20 seconds<sup>600f</sup>, delay 60~66.67 seconds<sup>1,800f~2,000f</sup>.
**2 [[Sir Seal]]s spawn after 30 seconds<sup>900f</sup>, delay 53.33~60 seconds<sup>1,600f~1,800f</sup>.
**5 [[Aku Gory|Aku Gories]] spawn after 33.33 seconds<sup>1,000f</sup>, delay 26.67~33.33 seconds<sup>800f~1,000f</sup>.
**Infinite [[Relic Doge]]s spawn after 53.33 seconds<sup>1,600f</sup>, delay 16.67~23.33 seconds<sup>500f~700f</sup>.
**1 [[Othom]] spawns after 120 seconds<sup>3,600f</sup>.
**1 [[Deathkory]] spawns after 50 seconds<sup>1,500f</sup>.

==Strategy==
Clear the Aku Doges, let your units bite the dust, then use the Cat Cannon to clear the field once the second Sir Seal spawns. Try to hit the base with [[Talents|Talented]] [[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Awakened Bahamut Cat]], that way you can chunk Berserkory and instantly eliminate him from the fight using the Cat Cannon thereafter. On {{2c}}, this won't be nearly enough damage to kill him, so cycle out a few [[Ancient Egg: N101 (Rare Cat)|Courier Cats]] alongside [[Kotatsu Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Octopus Cats]] to eat away at his remaining HP. Once he's dead, you can take things at a leisurely pace with [[Master Uril (Special Cat)|Esoteric Uril]] when it comes to chipping/piercing what's left of Le'Behemoth's Shield ([[Aku Researcher (Rare Cat)|Cat Researcher]] is recommended). Uril will do a fine job at holding the enemies in place until your Cat Cannon recharges, at which point you can wave goodbye to the first Le'Behemoth.

Deathkory will be a bigger problem, try to save your Cat Cannon for when he has his Shield down—he's less tanky than Berserkory without it. Despite the dangerous amount of enemies here, none of them are especially lethal in the way of pushing power, so [[Ancient Egg: N003 (Special Cat)|Cactus]]/[[Maize Cat (Rare Cat)|Cone Cats]] will generally do a good job at holding them back until you can use your Cat Cannon. The many enemies provide you with ample cash, so don't even worry about that much either, it's smooth sailing from here as long as you can properly wait out the Cat Cannon and use it with precision. As soon as Deathkory is dead, Le'Behemoth and Othom cannot do anything to ward off your inevitable advance.

